WEBVTT

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.583
Elephant!

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.167
Bear!

00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:29.917
Hide!

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:35.167
Darling! Darling!
Honeypot, I'm coming!

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.250
Honeypot! Honeypot!

00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:35.625
But it wasn't my fault.

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:37.958
Who else was in the house?
The door was locked.

00:01:38.042 --> 00:01:39.917
- There was an elephant.
- An elephant?

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:43.375
It had the head of an elephant and body
of a snake, but it tried to shoot me!

00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:45.417
- Have you been drinking salt water?
- No.

00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:47.708
Paddington, tell us
what really happened.

00:01:47.792 --> 00:01:49.292
- What?
- We won't be cross.

00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:52.875
- Speak for yourself.
- Mrs Brown, you must believe me.

00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:55.792
I would never lie to you.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.708
I'm sorry, but that was the last straw.

00:01:58.792 --> 00:02:00.333
It was an accident. They happen.

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:02.875
- But the children...
- Paddington's the best thing

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:05.583
that's ever happened to the children.
They're happy.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.500
But what's the point of them being happy
if they're not safe?

00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:10.000
He's putting them in danger.

00:02:10.042 --> 00:02:12.042
They have to be
our number-one priority.

00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.750
They are!

00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:17.333
They are.

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:24.292
And the worst part is
he won't even tell us the truth.

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:28.667
How can he live with us
if we can't even trust him?

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.583
I don't know, Henry.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.583
We've got to face facts.

00:02:33.292 --> 00:02:36.333
This house just isn't the place
for a bear.

00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:39.583
Perhaps you're right.

00:02:40.417 --> 00:02:43.000
Maybe we should take him
to the authorities.

00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:22.042
♪ Blow, wind, blow

00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:26.208
♪ Blow, wind, blow

00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:32.042
♪ I was never told the city of London
would be so cold

00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:22.875
Thank you.

00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:33.000
Get out of it!

00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:34.333
Bloody bears!

00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:38.250
♪ I decide to roam

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.875
♪ Now I wanted to go back home

00:04:48.625 --> 00:04:50.000
“Dear Browns.“

00:04:50.375 --> 00:04:55.000
"Thank you very much for having me
to stay. You are a very lovely family."

00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:59.417
"I'm very sorry
about the ﬂood and the fire...

00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:02.625
and the incident
at the Geographers' Guild."

00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:05.917
"I hope that...

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:10.500
now I have gone,
things will calm down a bit."

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.083
"Yours, Paddington."

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.208
Well, shall we go after him?

00:05:19.292 --> 00:05:21.458
It's better this way.

00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:23.833
He didn't really belong here.

00:05:23.917 --> 00:05:26.042
How can you say that?

00:05:28.458 --> 00:05:29.500
Judy.

00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:31.375
I'm going to my room.

00:05:32.917 --> 00:05:35.292
- Where are you going?
- I just...

00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:38.250
I need to know he's OK.

00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:48.000
You just don't get it, do you?

00:05:48.083 --> 00:05:49.208
What?

00:05:49.292 --> 00:05:54.250
This family needed that wee bear
every bit as much as he needed you.

00:05:55.583 --> 00:05:57.833
There. Said my piece.

00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:08.167
Hmm...

00:06:18.042 --> 00:06:21.292
Excuse me, I'm looking
for Montgomery Clyde.

00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:23.958
I'm sorry, mate, I'm Morgan Clyde.

00:06:24.042 --> 00:06:25.875
Ah. Thank you.

00:06:25.958 --> 00:06:27.542
He's about three foot six.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.917
He's got a bright red hat on
and a blue dufﬂe coat.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:34.750
And he's a bear.

00:06:36.375 --> 00:06:37.833
It's not much to go on.

00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:40.583
Really?

00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:42.833
Montgomery Clyde?

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:45.500
I'm Marjorie Clyde, dearie.

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:05.958
Still no news.

00:07:07.583 --> 00:07:09.292
In case you're interested.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:11.250
Right.

